1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,647
That label is built to be misread. Here is
the order that works.

2
00:00:06,197 --> 00:00:10,299
Twenty seconds is enough, if you read it
in the right order.

3
00:00:11,269 --> 00:00:12,775
Back of the pack first.

4
00:00:14,325 --> 00:00:20,641
Start at the serving size. Read the sugar
per serving. Two numbers, in that order.

5
00:00:21,611 --> 00:00:24,041
Ignore the front of the pack entirely.

6
00:00:25,591 --> 00:00:31,518
Per serving is a small number. Per pack is
the one you eat. The pack is the trap.

7
00:00:33,068 --> 00:00:39,200
One snack is twenty percent of your day.
One drink is thirty. It adds up fast.

8
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,599
One meal is fifty.

9
00:00:43,149 --> 00:00:46,415
Put it back, or buy one and stop at one.

10
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:51,696
Serving size, sugar, then ignore the
front.

11
00:00:53,246 --> 00:00:56,769
Turn the pack over. The answer is on the
back.
